WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:04.979
To tell the story of Gwyn's children is to tell the story of Gwyn himself.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.609
For his children were all born to fulfill a purpose.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.980
Gwyn's first daughter, Gwynevere, was a maternal figure cherished by all.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.280
She was born to soothe the kingdom after a period of intense war against the Dragons.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.540
Gwyn's son, Gwyndolin, was a master of illusion.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:31.120
After Gwynevere fled the failing kingdom in, fear it was Gwyndolin who disguised the fading of the light.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.660
And finally, Gwyn's youngest daughter, Filianore, was truly a product of her father's pride.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.060
For, as long as she slumbered, Gwyn's world would not end.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.880
But there was a fourth child a nameless king erased from history. The God of War.

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:51.539
Gwyn's firstborn son.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.400
The first war ever fought

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.360
was the war for disparity,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.580
a war for the right to flesh and blood where before there was only stone.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.100
A war for the right to the surface where before there was only the below.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:11.010
A war for the right to a beginning, and to an end, for before there was neither.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:16.619
The everlasting dragons were to be introduced to the concept of the end

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.580
And it was Gwyn's firstborn son, like his brothers and his sisters to come

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.520
who was divinely conceived for this purpose.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:32.340
So it was that the Sun's eldest born inherited the lightning from his father along with this powerful

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.980
predisposition for war and arms.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:40.229
His weapon was an ingenious sword-spear that leveraged the user's own bodyweight,

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.669
allowing it to be trodden remarkably deep into tough dragon hide;

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:52.229
this was the earliest form of what would become the cross spear which went on to inspire the

00:01:52.509 --> 00:01:56.549
legendary weapon wielded by the Dragonslayer Ornstein, who was,

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.200
unsurprisingly anointed the first Knight to the Nameless King himself.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.800
The Nameless King also wore an attire woven of sharp dragon scales, as they were themselves

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:13.040
impervious to fire, and it seems that the best tools against the Dragons

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.360
were taken from the Dragons themselves.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:23.400
A philosophy that another legendary figure, Havel, clearly took to heart as the man cased himself in stone

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.900
and took a legendary dragon tooth as his weapon.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:33.880
Havel too, not only served the Nameless King in the war, but also his first knight Ornstein as well.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:38.380
becoming the third member of a legendary trio of Dragon Slayers

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.620
who would eventually come to inspire the miraculous tale

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.700
known as "Sacred Oath."

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:52.360
And so, it was with strength, courage cunning and unity that the war for disparity was won.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.590
"Dragons"

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.760
"shall never be"

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.940
"forgotten. We Knights fought valiantly,"

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:03.819
"but for every one of them,"

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.880
"we lost three score of our own."

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.220
"Exhilaration,"

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.840
"Pride,"

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.440
"Hatred,"

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:13.860
"Rage."

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.420
"The dragons teased out our dearest emotions,"

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.840
"thou will understand, one day."

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.780
"Me?
There is very little to be said."

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.120
"What good is a dog, with no hares to hunt?"

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.940
"I am lucky to be alive, I suppose."

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.789
With the war won, these Lords were the first to face an uncomfortable truth

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:41.798
that their glory, much like that of the Dragons, would not last forever.

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:50.078
The everlasting dragons were vulnerable, now, and were forced to adapt to this unfamiliar and hostile world.

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:56.379
So they gave birth and slowly began to mutate and deviate in their evolution.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.919
Wyverns,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.700
serpents, man serpents, and basilisks.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.200
The imperfect, the crossbreeds, and the wretches.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.140
Dragons that spit fire, lightning, poison, and corrosion.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.940
Some even caught the undead curse.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.980
And, so it was that despite Gwyn's best efforts,

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:18.280
dragons and their kin lived on.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.120
Some, as unchanged as ever.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.220
"Rumor it may be but I have heard of a surviving ancient"

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.500
"dragon who resides in this land."

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.800
"A coterie of undead serves the dragon as they trained to become dragons themselves."

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.660
"Sounds unlikely,"

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.880
"but you never know, do you?"

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:42.040
As the gods really should have known, faith always finds a way,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.500
and ironically, it was the gods, and not the Dragons, who failed to adapt.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.959
A war had been fought in the name of disparity, but Gwyn's age of fire was nothing of the sort.

00:04:53.500 --> 00:05:00.000
Darkness was the enemy now, and Gwyn would do anything to prevent his age of fire from ending.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.620
Anything.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:08.920
So how righteous, truly, could their war against the ancient, unchanging dragons have been,

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:13.460
when Gwyn himself refused to cede to the natural order?

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:18.080
Thus began the betrayal of Gwyn's firstborn son,

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.960
his God of War who allied with the remaining ancient dragons.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.960
Ashamed by his firstborns betrayal,

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.500
enraged at his disobedience, and

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:34.900
driven by that famous desire to erase all that opposed him, Gwyn, disowned his firstborn son,

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.380
his royal blood was denied.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:41.280
His legacy was expunged from the annals of history,

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.160
and the altars of his worship were smashed beyond recognition.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.440
His name was lost forever.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:54.880
But as the gods ought to know, faith always finds a way, and the Nameless King had some faithful knights indeed.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:01.930
Look within the rubble of these statues; look amidst the traces of the Nameless King's foot wrappings;

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:08.199
His braces, his attire, and you might just spy a familiar cross spear design

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.180
belonging to the firstborn's first Knight:

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.100
The Dragonslayer Ornstein

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.280
In the dragonless age that followed the Nameless King's betrayal,

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.680
Ornstein was assigned to guard the Grand Cathedral.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:27.800
And for the captain of the Four Knights of Gwyn, this must have been a lowly role indeed,

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.640
as he wasn't even guarding Gwyn's daughter,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.220
he was guarding an illusion.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.300
Nor was he alongside his fellow Knights,

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.620
instead, he was partnered with

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:44.580
Executioner Smough, a cannibal and a glutton, someone who could never call himself Ornstein's equal.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:50.260
So as his fellow Knights faded away, as Gwyn burned to cinder for his age,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.800
Ornstein eventually left the ruined Cathedral and

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.240
abandoned his post in order to search for the nameless King that he once served.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.020
Funnily enough,

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:06.580
Smough, of all people, was the last Knight of Gwyn to remain at his post.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:09.680
We know this, for, after defeating Aldrich

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:17.700
we can purchase his armor, which implies that Smough the Cannibal, may well have been cannibalized himself,

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:25.100
an ironic twist of fate that Ornstein was lucky to avoid and we don't know exactly where or for how long

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.500
Ornstein set off in search of his nameless King.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:33.300
But if one attempted to trace his path, one would find evidence

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.720
of the influence that these two men may well have left upon the world.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:45.620
In Furossa, for example, we witness an order of Lion Knights with armour blessed by a certain war God.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:51.740
Even more curiously, the figure depicted on their helmet stands his own against a dragon.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.560
In the Drowned Ruins of Heide, there's a being who

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.580
aspires to the great legacy of the old Dragonslayer.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.920
So is this Ornstein himself?

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.740
Probably not, though...

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.360
How curious is it, that a man inspired by a dragonslayer

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:13.289
would be allied with the dragons that are right outside his gate?

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:19.380
The world was changing and, in truth, those who aspire to conquer dragons

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.640
overwhelmingly end up with them their allies.

00:08:23.199 --> 00:08:29.999
Look to our Nameless King, who was born for a war against them only to ally with the vestiges of their race.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:36.720
Look to Vendrick, who inherited Gwyn's legacy yet aspired to recreate their power.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:42.040
Look to the kingdom of Lothric, whose Knights were originally hunters of dragons,

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:45.800
yet they ended up taming them and fighting at their side.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.899
Look at Prince Ricard, who fought in a stronghold

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:54.600
filled with serpents and ended up being summoned as their champion at Arch Dragon Peak.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:59.280
Looked to Havel who adopted a spine of stone and a dragon's tooth,

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:03.520
only to uphold a sacred oath with their nameless King.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.060
And finally, look to Ornstein, the Dragonslayer,

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.860
who, laden with duties and oaths,

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:16.560
decided that the only one that would matter, was his pledge to Gwyn's exiled son.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:22.920
And so it was, that the Way of the Dragon led him to the Nameless King's stronghold.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:27.930
In the years after his exile, the Nameless King had tamed a Storm Drake,

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:31.420
upon which he had led a lifetime of battle.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.800
Eventually, he settled here, upon Archdragon Peak.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:39.320
This, it appears, was a place where dragons and their kin

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.320
could worship and live in peace.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:46.940
It was only a matter of time, after all, until Gwyn's Age of Fire would burn down to ash,

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:52.580
and dragons, as we know, have both time and patience in abundance.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:58.140
Alas. an Unkindled would eventually find his way here to Archdragon Peak,

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:03.740
driven, by this unstoppable desire to claim the strength of a War God,

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:06.400
and to claim the strength of his ancient

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:11.440
companions, so that Gwyn's Age of Fire could, finally, be brought to an end.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.920
For war is supposed to be waged for what we believe in,

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:19.080
not to erase our opposition from existence.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.500
*Ominous music fades out*

